<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>TransportX</title><link>https://transportxlab.com/</link><atom:link href="https://transportxlab.com/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><description>TransportX</description><generator>Hugo Blox Builder (https://hugoblox.com)</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Mon, 24 Oct 2022 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><image><url>https://transportxlab.com/media/icon_hu11734318148517933569.png</url><title>TransportX</title><link>https://transportxlab.com/</link></image><item><title>Traffic Agent</title><link>https://transportxlab.com/application/traffic-agent/</link><pubDate>Thu, 13 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://transportxlab.com/application/traffic-agent/</guid><description>&lt;p>Traffic Agent is a research prototype for transport analysis tasks. It brings data queries, map interaction, knowledge retrieval, and report drafting into one conversational workspace. Users can start with a specific transport question, inspect the relevant data and spatial evidence, and retain intermediate results during a multi-turn task.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>The Agent selects data, spatial-analysis, retrieval, and visualization tools according to the question. Its outputs are intended to support analysis and review rather than replace domain judgement.&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>CityWeave: Weaving User Needs and World Constraints for Personalized and Reliable Mobility Planning</title><link>https://transportxlab.com/publication/cityweave/</link><pubDate>Sat, 08 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://transportxlab.com/publication/cityweave/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="研究概览">研究概览&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>CityWeave 面向真实的门到门出行规划，同时考虑用户画像、时间窗口、地图拓扑和交通方式等约束。方法将规划过程拆解为 Who、When、Where 和 How 四个结构化槽位，再通过 User-World Grounding 模块检查个性化需求与导航可行性。&lt;/p>
&lt;h2 id="核心方法与发现">核心方法与发现&lt;/h2>
&lt;ul>
&lt;li>以 3W1H 结构约束多模态智能体的长链路推理和工具调用。&lt;/li>
&lt;li>联合优化用户偏好、地点存在性、路线连通性、换乘合法性和时刻表约束。&lt;/li>
&lt;li>在 18 万条真实出行规划记录上进行训练和评测，显著提升最终方案通过率、常识约束通过率、个性化和可靠性。&lt;/li>
&lt;/ul>
&lt;h2 id="资料来源">资料来源&lt;/h2>
&lt;ul>
&lt;li>&lt;a href="https://doi.org/10.1145/3770855.3818979" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ACM 论文 DOI&lt;/a>&lt;/li>
&lt;li>&lt;a href="https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/4rybhLtB3IxCyckLV2na6A" target="_blank" rel="noopener">TransportX Lab 公众号解读&lt;/a>&lt;/li>
&lt;/ul></description></item><item><title>TransportX at the 2026 Urban Transport Planning Annual Conference: AI and an Open, Collaborative Innovation Ecosystem</title><link>https://transportxlab.com/post/2026-urban-transport-planning-ai-ecosystem/</link><pubDate>Sat, 18 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://transportxlab.com/post/2026-urban-transport-planning-ai-ecosystem/</guid><description>&lt;p>TransportX participated in the 2026 Urban Transport Planning Annual Conference on July 17-18, 2026. Associate Professor Jian Li delivered a plenary presentation and joined the discussion at Forum 4, &amp;ldquo;An Open and Collaborative Transport Innovation Ecosystem.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p>
&lt;h2 id="july-17-plenary-presentation">July 17: plenary presentation&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>Associate Professor Jian Li presented &amp;ldquo;Working with AI: Building an Open and Collaborative Innovation Ecosystem for Urban Transport.&amp;rdquo; The presentation discussed a demand-led approach to AI agents in transport. It considered how scenario and operational understanding, model and tool systems, and data-access rules could jointly support open governance. Joint laboratories and governance sandboxes were presented as possible settings for testing practices that can later be adapted to other urban transport contexts.&lt;/p>
